problem:
From a point $\mathrm{P}\left(\mathrm{x}_{0}, \mathrm{y}_{0}\right)$ outside the parabola $\mathrm{y}^{2}=4 \mathrm{x}$, two tangents $P A$ and $P B$ are drawn, with $A$ and $B$ being the points of tangency.
(1) Express the area of $\triangle P A B$ in terms of $x_{0}, y_{0}$;
(2) If $\mathrm{P}\left(x_{0}, y_{0}\right)$ moves on the circle $(x+4)^{2}+y^{2}=9$, at what position of $\mathrm{P}$ is the area of $\triangle P A B$ maximized, and what is the maximum area?

